––– block: rejoin-diag –––
––– comment –––
Pause node 3 (the pid file holds the worker, not the watchdog) and wait until nodes 1 and 2 drop it from the view
––– input –––
P3=$(cat /var/log/manticore-3/searchd.pid); kill -STOP $P3; echo "node 3 stopped"
––– output –––
node 3 stopped
––– input –––
rj_wait "1306 2306" 60 '[ "$(rj_v 1306 nodes_view | tr , "\n" | grep -c :replication)" = 2 ] && [ "$(rj_v 2306 nodes_view | tr , "\n" | grep -c :replication)" = 2 ]'; echo "evicted $?"
––– output –––
evicted 0
––– comment –––
nodes_set still lists node 3; ALTER CLUSTER ADD asks every node of nodes_set for its state and a paused node holds the call up to 120 s, so drop node 3 from nodes_set first
––– input –––
rj_q 1306 "ALTER CLUSTER v1 UPDATE nodes"; mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "SHOW STATUS LIKE 'cluster_v1_nodes_set'\G" | grep Value
––– output –––
  Value: 127.0.0.1:1312,127.0.0.1:2312
